\section{Details}{
\link[storr:storr]{‘storr’} is a content addressed key-value store
with an optional caching layer.

The \code{storr_tiledb} generates a \link{TileDBStorr} object with identical
interface as \code{storr} that additionally supports
metadata next to key-values (notes and expiration timestamps) as well as asynchronous
writes using the \href{https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/mirai/index.html}{mirai}
framework.

\code{storr_tiledb()} and \code{storr(driver_tiledb())} can not be used interchangeably
if you use the extra features (i.e., expiration timestamps). The latter
is the standard storr interface and the former produces a stand-alone R6 class
that replicates the storr interface with additional features.

Another difference, but not visible to the user, is that the
\code{storr_tiledb}'s cache layer uses hash tables via \link[utils:hashtab]{hashtab()} instead of
environments.
\subsection{Cache option}{

The in-memory caching layer is enabled by default and is controlled via
the global option \code{storr.tiledb.cache} :

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode r">}}\preformatted{# Disable cache
 options(storr.tiledb.cache = FALSE)
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}

\subsection{Buffer size}{

The buffer allocation size is set to 3 MB per column when fetching data. Use
\code{\link[=set_allocation_size_preference]{set_allocation_size_preference()}} to set a different limit.
}

\subsection{Compression}{

The storage compression filter is \code{"ZSTD"} and is applied to dimensions, attributes,
coords and offsets. The compression level is configurable through \code{compression_level}
argument with default level \code{-7} that balances compression ratio and speed.

To create a driver without compression filters, set \code{compression_level = NULL}.

Note that a \code{"RLE"} filter is specifically used for validity bitmaps and is
not configurable. For more flexibility, see next section \verb{Schemas Configuration}.
}

\subsection{Schemas Configuration}{

To support different use cases with respect to speed and compression, a user
can create a custom driver schemas using the entry point functional wrapper
\code{\link[=driver_schemas]{driver_schemas()}}; this gives access to TileDB array schemas in the
content-addressable storage (CAS) system that can be modified in order to
tune TileDB's engine performance and storage characteristics: compression
algorithms, compression levels, tile and cell order. For details, see
\code{Examples} section.
}

\subsection{Async Evaluation}{

\code{storr_tiledb} uses \link[mirai:mirai]{mirai} package to set keys asynchronously. Async is
enabled either at initialisation or automatically when using one of the
async methods.

Each 'storr' instantiation comes with its own independent set of daemons using
a unique compute profile (namespace). To access the specific compute profile,
i.e., to launch more daemons via \code{mirai::launch_local()} use the active field
\verb{$async_info} :

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode r">}}\preformatted{# Retrieve mirai's compute profile
sto$async_info["profile"]

}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

By default, async process launches two daemons. This is configurable with
\code{storr.tiledb.mirai.daemons} option:

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode r">}}\preformatted{# set mirai daemons
 options(storr.tiledb.mirai.daemons = 1L)
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

In addition, to set a memory budget (in MB) for queued task payloads at the
dispatcher, use \code{storr.tiledb.mirai.memory} option:

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode r">}}\preformatted{# set mirai memory budget
 options(storr.tiledb.mirai.memory = 100) # 100MB
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

The daemons associated with the specific compute profile are reset to zero
when the 'storr' object is deleted/garbage collected.
}

\subsection{Key Expiration}{

Keys with expiration time-stamps are not automatically cleared; they can be
fetched post expiration datetime unless they are removed by using one of
\verb{$clear_expired_keys()} or \code{gc(clear_expired = TRUE)} method.

Alternatively, use \verb{$is_expired_key()} before a getter method for more refined
control.
}
}

